\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Comparison with staggered two-color determinants}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Hands, Kogut, Lombardo and Morrison study staggered
fermions with #{SU(2)} gauge fields and nonzero chemical
potential.
On printed p. 10 they use the pseudoreal matrix relation
to identify the determinant with its complex conjugate,
then assert positivity at nonzero chemical potential and
cite their reference [21], a private communication; see
\citet{§II, p. 10, and reference 21}{hands1999symmetries}.}

\p{That positivity assertion concerns the source's staggered
operator at nonzero chemical potential. The integral
cochain result \ref{fdip-00V6} instead has the displayed
perfect alternating Hurwitz form, the inverse-transport
adjoints, the degree proof of zero diagonal and the native
Pfaffian identities as its premises. The source paragraph
supplies no proof of those statements and no sign theorem
for a commuting-algebra label alone.}

\p{The finite calculations distinguish a complex line from
a real plane, a rank-#{4} modular fiber from a rank-two column
module, and a paired coefficient from an unpaired Pfaffian
construction. None of these algebraic distinctions selects
physical flavors, tastes or statistics.}
